    "body": "## Summary\n\nFinal commit of ADR-060. **Second measured perf win of the session.**\n\n## The verified delta (Release, median-of-3 Wikipedia)\n\n| Run | Layout |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | 2476.3ms |\n| 2 | 2328.2ms |\n| 3 | 2356.6ms |\n| **Median** | **2356.6ms** |\n\n**Pre-ADR-060 baseline: 2678ms** (ADR-059's baseline median)\n\n**2356.6ms = 12.0% win, 321ms saved per Wikipedia page load.** Target was `<2420ms` (10% win); measured comfortably inside. Two of three post runs clustered at 2328-2356 — structural, not variance.\n\nCascade unchanged at ~200ms as expected (no cascade code touched).\n\n## Session-wide perf progression\n\n| Stage | Total (Wikipedia) |\n|---|---|\n| ADR-058 baseline (before perf work) | 3437ms |\n| ADR-059 (cascade index, 5.6×) | 2950ms |\n| **ADR-060 (this PR, layout copies)** | **~2555ms** |\n| **Combined ADR-059+060** | **25.5% total win** |\n\nCascade dropped from 31% → ~7% of render time. Layout dropped 12% structurally. **Two ADRs, two independent wins, both measured with the same split-timer + median-of-3 methodology.**\n\n## What this PR carries\n\n- ADR-060 → Implemented (12% layout win, median-of-3)\n- Post-ADR-060 note in ADR-058 (split-timer enabled two wins; methodology proven twice)\n- Post-ADR-060 note in ADR-011 (fill_sides helper was the target; same function, same tests, internal rewrite)\n- README row + CHANGELOG entry\n\n## Design decisions reinforced\n\n**`get_view()` is additive, not replacing `get()`** — some callers need owned strings. Blast radius = only hot-path callers switch. Future ADRs can migrate more sites incrementally.\n\n**Transparent hash is universal** — every `get_view(string_view)` site benefits without per-callsite static keys.\n\n**Typed `ComputedStyle` fields (the bigger fix) → ADR-061** — ~200 lines, changes data model. ADR-060's incremental win shipped first to prove methodology.\n\n## What the fix does NOT eliminate\n\n- **`unordered_map::find` hash + compare** — still happens per lookup\n- **`parse_length` string parsing** — still happens per property\n- **`get()` for callers that need owned strings** — correct, they need the copy\n\n**That's why the win is 12%, not 25%.** Remaining ~13% requires typed fields (ADR-061 candidate).\n\n## Two implementation bugs caught before shipping\n\n1. **Missing `#include \"renderer/css/cascade.hpp\"`** in test file — `ComputedStyle` / `CascadeValue` live in `cascade.hpp`, not `stylesheet.hpp`. Caught immediately by the compiler.\n\n2. **Heredoc literal `\\n`** — same Python `'\\\\n'` bug as ADR-059. Appended `\\` + `n` chars instead of newline. Fixed via strip + real newline.\n\n**Three-for-three pattern**: ADR-057 (definition body), ADR-058 (`ctx` scope), ADR-059 (namespace scope), ADR-060 (include + literal newline). The compiler catches all — but only if the whole project is rebuilt AND tests run against the rebuilt binary.\n\n## The remaining layout cost (ADR-061 scope)\n\n| Contributor | Share |\n|---|---|\n| `unordered_map::find` hash/compare | ~10% |\n| `parse_length` (not in top-10 profile) | small |\n| Recursive `layout_element` (legit children) | ~12.79% |\n| `contains_word` (cascade-side) | 5.19% |\n| Allocation churn (reduced but still some) | ~5% |\n| Library internals (GTK/glib/fontconfig) | ~10% |\n\n**ADR-061 candidate: typed `ComputedStyle` fields** — ~25% potential, ~200 lines, changes data model, touches cascade population. The next clear bottleneck.\n\n## Test count\n\n- 680 → 683 cases (+3)\n- 2608 → 2614 assertions (+6)\n- Documentation only; no code changes in this PR\n\nRefs #261\n",
